-- | Error message bindings for the administrative layer (AccessControl /
-- Ownable-as-Admin-role / Pausable). Collected in one module so messages are
-- consistent and greppable; referenced from `assertMsg`. Each binding is
-- annotated with the invariant it enforces (see docs/ADMIN-LAYER-PLAN.md §7).
module SimpleToken.Admin.Errors where

-- Pausable
------------

-- | INV-25: gated factory origination choices must fail while the registry is paused.
eRegistryPaused : Text
eRegistryPaused = "simple-token: registry is paused"

-- | INV-26: pause/unpause must change the state (OpenZeppelin Pausable semantics —
-- `_pause`/`_unpause` revert when already in the target state). Avoids needless
-- factory recreation on no-op calls.
eRedundantPauseChange : Text
eRedundantPauseChange = "simple-token: registry already in the requested pause state"

-- Account freeze / compliance hold (AL-10)
-------------------------------------------

-- | INV-40: a frozen account is refused at every origination chokepoint — it can
-- neither send nor receive (nor be minted to). The per-account analogue of
-- `eRegistryPaused`; freeze is origination control like pause (it does not reach
-- into committed flows). The compliance hold is enforced by withholding the
-- registry admin's required signature at the factory, not via a public blocklist.
eAccountFrozen : Text
eAccountFrozen = "simple-token: account is frozen (compliance hold)"

-- | INV-42: freezing an already-frozen account is rejected (non-idempotent, like
-- `eRedundantPauseChange`), so the frozen-set stays duplicate-free.
eAccountAlreadyFrozen : Text
eAccountAlreadyFrozen = "simple-token: account is already frozen"

-- | INV-42: unfreezing an account that is not frozen is rejected.
eAccountNotFrozen : Text
eAccountNotFrozen = "simple-token: account is not frozen"

-- | INV-42: the registry administrator party cannot be frozen — freezing the root
-- would brick every gated flow (it co-signs every holding and originates supply).
eCannotFreezeAdmin : Text
eCannotFreezeAdmin = "simple-token: the registry administrator cannot be frozen"

-- AccessControl (capabilities)
--------------------------------

-- INV-27 (admin gate), INV-28 (assignee / anti-impersonation), and INV-29 (role
-- gate) are now enforced by the decoupled OpenZeppelin AccessControl library
-- (`OpenZeppelin.AccessControl.requireRole`), which owns their messages — see
-- SimpleToken.Admin.Capability.requireRole (AL-7). The token retains only the
-- gates the minimal primitive does not cover.

-- | INV-30: a capability is only honored when its scope authorizes the operation.
eCapabilityScopeMismatch : Text
eCapabilityScopeMismatch = "simple-token: capability scope does not authorize this operation"

-- | INV-31: a capability presented for revocation must have been issued by this registry.
eCapabilityNotIssuedByThisAdmin : Text
eCapabilityNotIssuedByThisAdmin = "simple-token: capability was not issued by this registry administrator"

-- | INV-31 (AL-8): the `Admin`/`DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE` is root-managed and is NOT
-- issuable or revocable through the delegated role-admin path — even by another
-- `Admin` holder (the `AccessControlDefaultAdminRules` posture; preserves safety
-- decision C9: no free re-delegation of root). `Admin` moves only via the genesis
-- root (`Admin_IssueRole`/`Admin_RevokeRole`) or the two-step + timelocked
-- default-admin handoff. The carve-out is the single-source
-- `SimpleToken.Admin.Roles.delegableViaRoleAdmin` predicate, enforced once in the
-- shared `SimpleToken.Admin.Authority.requireRoleAdmin` chokepoint; every other
-- role is administered through its `roleAdmin`.
eDefaultAdminRoleRootManaged : Text
eDefaultAdminRoleRootManaged = "simple-token: the Admin role is root-managed and cannot be delegated (use the timelocked handoff)"

-- Supply management (mint / burn — AL-5/AL-6)
----------------------------------------------

-- | INV-35: a mint must be for a positive amount of a supported instrument.
eMintAmountNotPositive : Text
eMintAmountNotPositive = "simple-token: mint amount must be positive"

-- | INV-36 (D3): a capped Minter capability cannot mint beyond its remaining allowance.
eMintAllowanceExceeded : Text
eMintAllowanceExceeded = "simple-token: mint exceeds the Minter capability's remaining allowance"

-- | A capped-minter allowance must be non-negative.
eMintAllowanceNegative : Text
eMintAllowanceNegative = "simple-token: mint allowance must be non-negative"

-- | INV-36 (D3): a capped Minter must mint atomically into a pre-authorized
-- recipient (preapproval-direct path). The proposal (cold-recipient) path splits
-- the mint across two transactions controlled by different parties and so cannot
-- atomically enforce/decrement the allowance — it is restricted to unlimited
-- minters. See docs/ADMIN-LAYER-PLAN.md §11.
eCappedMinterRequiresPreapproval : Text
eCappedMinterRequiresPreapproval = "simple-token: a capped Minter must mint via the recipient's preapproval (no proposal path)"

-- | Reconciling supply must not drive the advisory total negative.
eSupplyWouldGoNegative : Text
eSupplyWouldGoNegative = "simple-token: total-supply adjustment would go negative"
